+ *
+ * Newlines go too: \n\n+ becomes </p><p> further down, which would put
+ * broken markup inside the <pre>. &#10; renders as a line break in a <pre>.
+ *
+ * ONE pass, not six chained replaces. Chaining re-scans its own output: the
